From: openHC <noreply@openhc>
Subject: [PATCH] GLContextLibWPE: hand the PowerVR LinuxFB WSEGL a 0 native window

WebKit's GLContext::create() treats the native-window handle as a flag:
`window ? createWindowContext() : createOffscreenContext()`. A WPE view backend
must therefore return a NON-ZERO native window for the compositor to get a real
on-screen (window) GL context rather than an offscreen one.

The Imagination DDK's LinuxFB WSEGL, however, exposes a single surface -- the
framebuffer -- and accepts ONLY a 0 native-window handle; eglCreateWindowSurface
with any other value fails (EGL_NO_SURFACE), leaving the compositor with no
context and nothing ever reaching /dev/fb0.

wpebackend-pvr resolves the flag side by returning a non-zero sentinel from
get_native_window; this resolves the EGL side by ignoring that sentinel in the
one place the WPE window surface is actually created and passing the WSEGL the 0
it requires. Only affects the USE(WPE_RENDERER) LinuxFB path.

--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/egl/GLContextLibWPE.cpp	2026-10-06 16:44:47
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/egl/GLContextLibWPE.cpp	2026-10-06 16:44:47
@@ -56,7 +56,13 @@
     // EGLNativeWindowType changes depending on the EGL implementation, reinterpret_cast
     // would work for pointers, and static_cast for numeric types only; so use a plain
     // C cast expression which works in all possible cases.
-    return eglCreateWindowSurface(display, config, (EGLNativeWindowType) window, nullptr);
+    // openHC: the PowerVR SGX LinuxFB WSEGL exposes a single surface (the framebuffer)
+    // and accepts ONLY a 0 native-window handle; any other value fails surface creation.
+    // But WebKit's GLContext uses the handle as a flag (window ? createWindowContext :
+    // createOffscreenContext), so wpebackend-pvr must return a non-zero sentinel to get a
+    // window context at all. Reconcile here: ignore the sentinel, hand the WSEGL its 0.
+    (void) window;
+    return eglCreateWindowSurface(display, config, (EGLNativeWindowType) 0, nullptr);
 }
 
 std::unique_ptr<GLContext> GLContext::createWPEContext(GLDisplay& display, EGLContext sharingContext)
